# Global gitignore — applies to every repo on this machine.
# Set via: git config --global core.excludesfile ~/.gitignore_global
#
# Scope: machine/tool litter that no project should have to defend against
# individually. Project-specific ignores still belong in the repo's .gitignore.

# --- MCP server litter ---------------------------------------------------
# Several MCP servers open their logfile at a RELATIVE path, so it lands in
# whatever CWD the stdio process inherits. Claude Code spawns them with the
# session's working directory, so these seed themselves into any repo you
# happen to be working in. (Observed: mcp-excalidraw-server, 5 copies.)
excalidraw.log
mcp-*.log

